I'd like to propose a Sporkhack pirate class. Yes, this class has been
proposed on numerous occasions. I simply think a pirate class would
blend nicely with some of the new Spork ideas proposed, such as rusty
weaponry inducing disease, and the 'stealthy' aspect of knives. In
particular, a pirate could take special advantage of *water*.

Starting equipment: oilskin cloak, grappling hook, flail (so the hook
is immediately useful!), four-seven +1 knives, cram rations, and
potions of booze and oil. I mean, he's not a proper stinky pirate
without the booze. Pet is a monkey that steals for you, and can reach
a higher level than a normal monkey. Maybe a "capuchin" or some
special kind of monkey.

Special skills: what separates him from a rogue or ranger? Well, in
the early game, he's stronger in melee and weaker in ranged combat.
And he gets a grappling hook and the advantage of a *silent* ranged
attack. In the late game, he has special control over water.

Quest: Your quest leader is Jack Sparrow, a marked man who needs you
to get the Heart of Davy Jones to further his currently dubious
bargaining position with Jones. See, he's a bit afraid of water at the
moment, and *the quest artifact is underwater*, so he dare not get the
Heart himself. Jack gives you an amulet of magical breathing in order
to face him, meaning you *can't wear amulets of reflection or life
saving when facing Jones*, unless you become undead.

The setting is a haunted, beached pirate ship. The quest monsters are
sea monsters, and skeletons wielding rusty scimitars. Disease,
anyone? ;)

Quest Artifact: The Heart of Davy Jones allows you control of water.
When carried, it confers unbreathing and possibly regeneration. When
invoked, it creates several pools of water next to you, giving you a
*really* powerful escape mechanism and a semi-reliable instakill for
breathing monsters.

Alternate quest artifact: a cursed gold ring that grants you undead
characteristics such as hungerless regeneration, death resistance
(*not* magic resistance, but a decent substitute), and unbreathing -
but *only* when you're surrounded by darkness, e.g. the planes,
Astral, and Gehennom. Yes, I know it's the bastard child of "Pirates
of the Carribean" plot devices, but I think it's cool. And it
prohibits jumping in a way.  =)

Quest Boss: The dreaded Davy Jones, generated for away from the
upstairs *underwater*. Can summon Krakens rather than the usual
nasties. However, he's quite weak on land, so you must find a way to
get to the only dry land on the level near the upstairs.

Since you risk blanking scrolls of teleportation you take to the
water, you will *need* teleport control and a wand of teleport, or a
drum of earthquake so you can wake him from the upstairs.
Alternatively, use scrolls of earth, wands of cold, or water walking
to get close to him. Quaff a cursed !gain level after beating on him,
etc. He seems like a fun boss to me.

Titles: Landlubber, Powder Monkey, ... , Pirate King/Queen

